  "architecture_decision": "Build a bounded search service that derives visible leads first through the centralized VIEW policy, then searches party identity, aliases, normalized contact identifiers, lead numbers, and authorized activity/task text. Use exact identifiers first, normalized text and PostgreSQL full-text/trigram annotations when PostgreSQL is active, and deterministic Python fallback ranking for the test backend. Return match reasons and stable cursors without exposing out-of-scope rows, counts, or snippets.",
